# A100 deployment parameters (A100, 80 GB or 40 GB, compute capability 8.0): configs/h100.env's parameters — the same variables, probes, refusals and
# JIT-cache keying (MODEL_OPT_STACK_KEY is derived from the running stack on either card: torch2.6.0-cu124-sm80 here) — with this card's one
# value, the target-GPU word, set first. The mode and the variant are NOT here (`--mode` / `--variant`, CALIBY_OPT / CALIBY_VARIANT).
# Nothing here or in the kit is sized by the card's memory: both A100 sizes source this same file and run the same rows; what a run needs follows the
# input's residue count and upstream's batch knobs (--batch_size, --pp_batch_size), README.md Notes "Cards" — an out-of-memory error is raised, never a fallback.
# usage: `run.sh design|check|warm --config a100 --mode <mode> ...`, or `source configs/a100.env` before calling the package or upstream's
# scripts directly. The activation and check lines compare the word with the box's GPU by name and report a mismatch, never refuse.
export MODEL_OPT_TARGET_GPU=${MODEL_OPT_TARGET_GPU:-A100}                                                            # the GPU this configuration targets (compute capability 8.0); the activation and check lines report a mismatch with the box's GPU (never a refusal)
. "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")/h100.env"                                                                            # keep this line last: configs/h100.env's refusals (its return codes) are this file's
